s read (not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the row is formed). A struct rather than a lazy map, so an algorithm that keeps an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator per vertex on its stack (Tarjan’s) allocates nothing for it."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Successors"}]},"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"text":" whose out-neighbors come from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure, called on demand and never stored: an implicit graph (Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grid_graph"},{"text":", LEMON’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GridGraph"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FullGraph"},{"text":"). It is a lawful ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":", so every generic algorithm runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on it, including those that need the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]}}}